        <oboInOwl:id>CMO:0000750</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>The term &quot;absolute change&quot; refers to the subtraction of one value from another, as opposed to a dissimilarity of two values expressed as a ratio or as a percentage. In this context it is not intended to necessarily imply the difference expressed as an absolute value |n|, that is, the numeric value of the difference without regard to its sign.</rdfs:comment>
