            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A role in human social processes that inheres in an organism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117 xml:lang="en">William R. Hogan
Mathias Brochhausen</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/omrse.owl"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defined class that we will ultimately move to an application ontology.  We are leaving here for now until we determine which application ontology: it is likely going to be an ontology that does not currently (2012-06-05) exist.

Ditto for its current descendants.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Includes animals as well as humans.  For example, pet, assistance animal, animal grown for food, work animal, domesticated animal, K-9, etc.  Human roles include gender role, party to legal entities, health care provider roles like doctor, nurse, etc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Previous definition: A role in human social processes played by an organism.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">organism social role</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


